From 007c1af504855ec4c6dd04a37c46fd96612e243d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:43:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: retire clients and contexts before parent
 removal

Parent removal clears driver data before managed child removal calls
qcom_iommu_ctx_remove(), which reads that parent pointer. It also forces
suspend before unregistering clients that can still need their contexts.
Unregister clients while their context banks and PM are available, remove
the sysfs representation, explicitly release managed children, then force
suspend and clear parent data. Automatic devres cleanup must not remove
the already released children a second time.

The extracted probe-tail/remove and LTS cleanup model reproduces 24 wrong
cases out of 30 before the changes and none out of 36 afterward, including
six new PM cleanup-action allocation failures. Three wrong orderings fail
their intended contracts. Pre-tail allocation/resource getters, devres
list storage, device creation, client release, PM transitions and hardware
are modeled. Invalid parent access is intercepted before dereference;
full driver-core registration, locking and concurrency are not executed.

Three native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT driver objects compile cleanly with
nonpermissive CFI and match current source checksums. All other driver
functions, board data and schemas retain their prior bytes. These new
local repairs are prepared by Codex; human DCO and security/owner review
remain pending. No sign-off certification or physical acceptance is made.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index ff134563dad9..e94be05ec5db 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -1149,10 +1149,13 @@ static void qcom_iommu_device_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/* Retire clients while their context banks and parent PM are available. */
+	iommu_device_unregister(&qcom_iommu->iommu);
+	iommu_device_sysfs_remove(&qcom_iommu->iommu);
+	devm_of_platform_depopulate(&pdev->dev);
+
 	pm_runtime_force_suspend(&pdev->dev);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, NULL);
-	iommu_device_sysfs_remove(&qcom_iommu->iommu);
-	iommu_device_unregister(&qcom_iommu->iommu);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
-- 
2.56.0

